{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he trusted in HaShem.</b> He trusted that He would do what He said without any doubt, even though the matter was impossible or remote according to nature." "<b>And He reckoned it to him as righteousness.</b> The blessed El reckoned this trust in Him as righteousness and merit for Abraham. By this He made known that when Abraham afterward said, <b>By what shall I know that I shall inherit it?</b>, he did not retract his faith at all — for had he done so, his faith would not have been reckoned as righteousness at all, as it says: וּבְשׁוּב צַדִּיק מִצִּדְקָתוֹ וְעָשָׂה עָוֶל כָּל צִדְקוֹתָיו אֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה לֹא תִזָּכַרְנָה (Ezekiel 18:24)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:16.901478839Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}